+ G on your keyboard. This will ensure your entire flowchart is grouped, making it easier to copy. Once you\u2019ve made your selection, click the flowchart and hit Command + C on your keyboard or right-click and hit Copy."," "]}),(0,n.jsxs)("p",{children:["If you want to copy individual objects or symbols on your flowchart, click the item you want to copy and hit Command + C on your keyboard, or right-click and hit Copy."," "]}),(0,n.jsxs)("p",{children:["You can also make a copy of your flowchart for others to use by adding it to the"," ",(0,n.jsx)(tJ.N,{href:"https://www.figma.com/community/",children:"Figma Community"}),". To do this, click the Share button in the top right corner of your board, then click Publish to Community. You must have \u201CCan edit\u201D access to publish the file to the Community."," "]}),(0,n.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,n.jsx)(tJ.N,{href:"https://help.figma.com/hc/articles/360040035974-Publish-files-to-the-Community",children:"Learn more about how to publish files to the Figma Community"}),"."," "]})]}),(0,n.jsxs)("details",{className:t1,children:[(0,n.jsxs)("summary",{children:[(0,n.jsx)("span",{className:t2,id:"59-can-i-create-a-flowchart-with-specific-symbols-on-my-online-whiteboard",children:"Can I create a flowchart with specific symbols on my online whiteboard?"}),(0,n.jsx)(tZ.k,{className:t5})]}),(0,n.jsxs)("p",{children:["Absolutely! Flowchart symbols are shapes, lines, and arrows that represent actions or processes on your flowchart diagram. For example, a diamond shape symbolizes points where decisions are made, rectangles signify a specific action or step needed to carry out a process, and parallelograms show where users input or output data."," "]}),(0,n.jsxs)("p",{children:["FigJam\u2019s online whiteboard has over 20 shapes and symbols you can use to build a flowchart that maps user flows, systems, and processes. Read FigJam\u2019s"," ",(0,n.jsx)(tJ.N,{href:"https://www.figma.com/resource-library/flowchart-symbols/",children: